# Git workflow — ezoato / zovu-project

**Remote:** `https://github.com/Donchaminade/ezoato.git`

## Branches

| Branch | Role |
|--------|------|
| `master` | Production — **never push or commit directly** |
| `dev` | Integration — default target for all PRs |
| `feature/*`, `fix/*`, `chore/*` | Short-lived work branches |

## Flow

1. `git checkout dev && git pull origin dev`
2. `git checkout -b feature/<slug>` (or `fix/`, `chore/`)
3. Commit, push branch, open PR **into `dev`**
4. After review and validation on `dev`, promote to production: PR or merge **`dev` → `master`** only for releases

## Commits

- Imperative subject, ≤72 chars: `feat(mobile): improve account shell navigation`
- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`
- No secrets (`.env`, `config.local.php`, credentials)

## Agent behavior

- Always branch from `dev`; never commit on `master`
- Never `git push origin master` for feature work
- Never force-push `master`
- Before commit: confirm `.env` and local secrets are not staged

## PR checklist

- [ ] Tests / manual check on target platform (web + mobile if touched)
- [ ] Lint/analyze clean where applicable
- [ ] No secrets in diff
- [ ] PR base branch is `dev` (not `master`)
